2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0277
HOUSE BILL NO. HB0168
Cultivated meat-prohibition.
Sponsored by: Representative(s) Eklund, Banks, Brady and
Davis and Senator(s) Crago and Driskill
A BILL
for
1 AN ACT relating to public health and safety; prohibiting
2 the manufacture, sale and distribution of cultivated meat;
3 providing definitions; providing penalties; and providing
4 for effective dates.
5
6 Be It Enacted by the Legislature of the State of Wyoming:
7
8 Section 1. W.S. 35-7-110(a) by creating a new
9 paragraph (xxxii) and by renumbering paragraph (xxxii) as
10 (xxxiii), 35-7-111(a) by creating a new paragraph (xiv) and
11 35-7-125(a) are amended to read:
12
13 35-7-110. Definitions.
14
15 (a) As used in this act:
1 HB0168

2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0277
1
2 (xxxii) "Cultivated meat" means meat that is
3 grown entirely in a laboratory from cultured animal cells
4 rather than harvested from an animal;
5
6 (xxxii) (xxxiii) "This act" means W.S. 35-7-109
7 through 35-7-126.
8
9 35-7-111. Prohibited acts.
10
11 (a) No person shall:
12
13 (xiv) Manufacture for sale, sell, offer for sale
14 or distribute for sale cultivated meat in this state.
15
16 35-7-125. Summary suspension of a license.
17
18 (a) A regulatory authority may summarily suspend a
19 license to operate a food establishment if it determines
20 through consultation with a health officer, inspection,
21 examination of food, employees, records or other authorized
22 means that an establishment is manufacturing for sale,
23 selling, offering for sale or distributing for sale
2 HB0168

2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0277
1 cultivated meat or an imminent health hazard exists
2 including, but not limited to, fire, flood, extended
3 interruption of electrical or water service, or sewage
4 backup.
5
6 Section 2. The department of agriculture shall
7 promulgate all rules necessary to implement this act.
8
9 Section 3.
10
11 (a) Except as otherwise provided by subsection (b) of
12 this section, this act is effective July 1, 2025.
13
14 (b) Sections 2 and 3 of this act are effective
15 immediately upon completion of all acts necessary for a
16 bill to become law as provided by Article 4, Section 8 of
17 the Wyoming Constitution.
